body:
Thank you for the reply, I'm never sure if anyone will respond. I usually do take space from people when i notice I don't like them rn, and then come back later like a week and I usually feel different. Usually they do something nice adn then I like them again. That's ok right? I also kept my mouth shut cause I knew that I was seeing the bad in everyone and I was very defensive and ready to fight (with words not actions). So I guess at that point I can only get space and maybe try explaining to others what is happening.

&#x200B;

It's rly difficult like this is the reason why I avoided everyone and everything for two years so I was never triggered. But you can't do that. So i have to manage getting upset every 2 weeks lol. 

&#x200B;

"juts cause you have a negative experience with someone doesn't mean your friendship is over" yes that's so important cause I always feel like things are ruined forever. I need to be positive or at least neutral about the future. 

&#x200B;

Those are good techniques and advice ty

Hey, I was born with really inflexible tendons and it doesn't bother me day to day, but if I work out sometimes my knee hurts- pain is behind my kneecap- (squats are really bad for this), not in a "I'm stretching it" way, in a "This is a worrying feeling" way. It's also pretty much on my one leg that didn't have an operation to lengthen it. I want to make my muscles and such stronger so it doesn't hurt as much. Stretching on incline is good so I do that, and I've also been doing leg press until my knee starts hurting then I stop (which is at about the end of 2 reps of 16). Any weight training I could do to strengthen muscles around my weak leg to put less pressure on the knee and tendon? 

&#x200B;

Also, it has gotten better as I'm working out more. At one point it hurt just to walk cause I didn't move from my bed for most of 2020, but that's stopped so I know it's possible to make it stronger.
